    val stories = listOf(
        StorySeries("the_city_of_small_promises", "The City of Small Promises", "A young volunteer follows a trail of handwritten promises and helps a city restore a forgotten public space.", listOf(
            StoryPart(1, "The First Card", listOf("On the first day of the school break, Eniola volunteered at the neighbourhood information desk. Behind its counter she found a jar filled with folded cards, each carrying a promise someone had made to the community.", "The oldest card read: 'We will bring the garden back.' It was signed only with the letter M, and dated twenty-two years earlier.")),
            StoryPart(2, "A Garden Without a Map", listOf("The council map showed no garden, only a paved lot beside the old cinema. Eniola asked the caretaker, who remembered trees there before the cinema was built.", "He said the residents had planted them together, but the project ended when the land was reassigned. He could not remember who had kept the original agreement.")),
            StoryPart(3, "The Cinema Ticket", listOf("Inside an old ticket tin, Eniola found a photograph of the garden opening. A woman in the picture held a folder marked 'shared land use'.", "Her friend Malik recognised the woman as his grandmother's former neighbour, Mrs Madu. He offered to ask whether she still had the folder.")),
            StoryPart(4, "Mrs Madu's Folder", listOf("Mrs Madu remembered the garden clearly. She had kept copies of meeting notes, but the pages were scattered between recipe books and family photographs.", "The notes showed that the garden was meant to be temporary until a permanent site could be approved. The residents had never received the council's final response.")),
            StoryPart(5, "The Unsent Reply", listOf("At the council archive, Eniola found a reply addressed to the garden committee. It had been returned because the committee's meeting address was written incorrectly.", "The letter approved a permanent garden on a different plot, but the notice never reached the residents. That plot was now a small paved square beside the library.")),
            StoryPart(6, "A New Location", listOf("The library manager confirmed that the square was underused and could be considered for a garden. The council required a fresh proposal, including access, maintenance, and a clear public benefit.", "Eniola and Malik invited the old committee members to help. Some were surprised that their plan had not been rejected after all.")),
            StoryPart(7, "The Promise Jar", listOf("They opened the jar and sorted the cards by topic. Some promised books, some promised music lessons, and several offered to help maintain a garden.", "The cards were not contracts, but they showed that many people still cared. Eniola copied them into a community archive and invited each writer to renew or update their offer.")),
            StoryPart(8, "A Plan with Roots", listOf("The group designed a small garden with accessible paths, shaded seats, and containers that could be moved if the library needed the space. A horticulture teacher checked the plant list.", "The council asked for proof that the garden would not block the emergency route. Malik measured the space with the library manager and revised the layout.")),
            StoryPart(9, "The Cost of Keeping It", listOf("The first budget was too high. Rather than abandon the idea, the group asked local nurseries about donated seedlings and reused containers.", "A builder offered leftover safe paving materials, while the library agreed to provide water. The budget became smaller and easier to maintain.")),
            StoryPart(10, "The Missing Signature", listOf("The council returned the application because one original committee signature was missing. The signer, Mr Afolayan, had moved away and was difficult to contact.", "Mrs Madu found an old postcard with his new town. Eniola wrote a respectful letter explaining the project and included copies of the original minutes.")),
            StoryPart(11, "A Reply from Far Away", listOf("Mr Afolayan replied with the signed page and a note saying he was glad the plan had survived. He also shared a photograph of the garden's first planting day.", "The group added the photograph to the archive and submitted the complete application. For the first time, the project had both its history and a practical present-day plan.")),
            StoryPart(12, "The Review Meeting", listOf("At the council review, residents explained why the garden mattered and how they would look after it. The library manager described how it could support reading and outdoor learning.", "A councillor asked what would happen if volunteers stopped coming. Eniola presented a rota with backup teams and a small annual maintenance allowance.")),
            StoryPart(13, "A Conditional Yes", listOf("The council approved a six-month trial, provided the garden remained accessible and the group reported on maintenance. The team accepted the conditions and chose coordinators for each task.", "Eniola worried that six months was not enough to prove the idea. Mrs Madu reminded her that a careful beginning was better than a promise nobody could keep.")),
            StoryPart(14, "The First Planting", listOf("Families arrived with seedlings, gloves, and reused pots. The horticulture teacher showed the children how to plant carefully and label each container.", "Malik installed the signs, while Eniola placed a weatherproof copy of the garden rules near the entrance. The square looked different by sunset.")),
            StoryPart(15, "A Week of Dry Weather", listOf("The first week brought unusually hot weather. Several plants struggled, and the group realised their watering rota was not detailed enough.", "They adjusted the schedule, added shade cloth where appropriate, and asked the nursery for advice. The setback became a lesson recorded for future volunteers.")),
            StoryPart(16, "The Open Book Bench", listOf("The library donated a weatherproof bench and a small shelf for books that could be read outdoors. Residents began using the space during lunch breaks.", "A retired teacher offered a weekly reading hour, and a local artist volunteered to paint a simple sign. The garden was becoming more than a planting project.")),
            StoryPart(17, "The Promise Renewed", listOf("The information desk received new cards. One child promised to water the seedlings on Saturdays; a shopkeeper promised to lend tools; a teacher offered to run a science activity.", "Eniola made sure each promise had a named coordinator and a realistic schedule. She had learned that kindness worked best when people knew exactly how to help.")),
            StoryPart(18, "The Six-Month Review", listOf("The council inspected the garden and found that the paths were clear, the plants were maintained, and the library had hosted regular activities. Residents presented photographs and a simple record of costs.", "The trial had met its conditions. The council offered a longer agreement, with a review each year and a small fund for repairs.")),
            StoryPart(19, "The Last Old Card", listOf("At the celebration, Mrs Madu brought the oldest card from the jar. She revealed that the letter M belonged to her late brother, who had first proposed the garden.", "She placed the card in the library archive beside the original approval letter. The group agreed to keep the jar at the information desk for future ideas.")),
            StoryPart(20, "A City That Keeps Its Word", listOf("The garden's anniversary brought together the people who had planted the first trees and the children who now cared for the new space. Eniola read the first card aloud and then read a new promise written by the youngest volunteer.", "The old garden could not be rebuilt exactly where it once stood, but its purpose had returned in a place that served the whole neighbourhood. The records were preserved, the council agreement was secure, and the promises had become practical work. Eniola understood that a city was not made trustworthy by grand speeches; it was made trustworthy when ordinary people kept small promises together."))
        ))
    )
